# Runtime profile: local or test. Fake providers are rejected unless this is test.
GRAPHME_PROFILE=local
GRAPHME_DATA_DIR=.graphme
# Optional non-secret YAML file. Provider credentials are rejected in YAML.
# GRAPHME_CONFIG=graphme.yaml

# The chat model: GRAPHME_PROVIDER is openai, anthropic or gemini, and its key is read from
# that provider's own variable only -- never from a YAML file. Leave the model and the
# address unset for the provider's default. The model has to take images and answer to a
# JSON schema. Anthropic has no embeddings: searching needs an OpenAI or a Gemini key too.
GRAPHME_PROVIDER=openai
OPENAI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GRAPHME_MODEL=
# GRAPHME_MODEL_BASE_URL=

# The embedder: one for the whole product -- the graph space (embed-graph, ask, the web app) and
# the one-document path (ingest, query) alike. Left unset it is the chat provider's own when that
# provider has one, else openai, and its key is that provider's variable. Passages are sent to
# the provider to be embedded.
# GRAPHME_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# GRAPHME_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-large
# GRAPHME_EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=3072

# Browser OOXML rendering. LibreOffice was removed on 2026-09-11; DOCX, PPTX and XLSX
# are drawn by a WASM parser on a Canvas, and an XLSX sheet maps 1:1 to a page.
# Build the viewer bundle once:
#   src/graphme/adapters/rendering/viewer/setup.sh
# Both are optional -- left unset, the bundle is read from the cache path below and
# Playwright's own Chromium is used (`python -m playwright install chromium --only-shell`). setup.sh builds into GRAPHME_VIEWER_DIR when it is set here.
# GRAPHME_VIEWER_DIR=~/.cache/graphme/ooxml-viewer
# GRAPHME_CHROME_EXECUTABLE=/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
# GRAPHME_RENDER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300

# Outline derivation for `graphme ingest` (one document). "off" stores no outline; "derived"
# reads the outline from the rendered page and costs one model call per page. The demo and
# `graphme build-graph` always derive it.
# GRAPHME_HIERARCHY_MODE=off

# How many independent readings each page gets. Above one they run together, and where
# they disagree the model is shown both readings beside the page and keeps one -- that
# second opinion costs one extra call only when the readings actually differ.
# Unset, `graphme ingest` and `build-graph` read once and the demo twice.
# GRAPHME_HIERARCHY_READINGS=1

# The graph space: one Neo4j every document of a corpus is put in (`graphme build-graph`).
# Nothing to set up: when nothing answers at the address below, the first use starts a
# Neo4j container (`graphme-neo4j`, Docker needed) on its port, with no password, open to this
# machine only, its data kept in the `graphme-neo4j-data` volume. A Neo4j of someone else's there
# that wants a password (Neo4j Desktop, brew) is left alone unless a password is set below: ours
# is started on the first free port after it. Set these only to use a Neo4j you
# run yourself; a password is read from the environment only, never from a YAML file.
# Aura's instance, user and password are asked for only when uploading to it.
# GRAPHME_NEO4J_URI=bolt://127.0.0.1:7687
# GRAPHME_NEO4J_USER=neo4j
# GRAPHME_NEO4J_PASSWORD=
# Memory of the Neo4j started here (heap, page cache). The page cache holds the passages'
# vectors: for thousands of documents give it at least their size, and give Docker's VM
# that much more. Changed, the container is made again on the same data.
# GRAPHME_NEO4J_HEAP=1g
# GRAPHME_NEO4J_PAGECACHE=512m

# The HTTP server (`graphme serve`). Set, every /v1 request must carry it (Authorization:
# Bearer <key>, or the web app's cookie). Empty, nothing is asked -- and the server opens on
# this machine (127.0.0.1) only; it is required to open it to anything else.
GRAPHME_API_KEY=

# Retrieval limits.
GRAPHME_RETRIEVAL_TOP_K=8
# How near (cosine, 0-1) a passage must be to the question to be kept by meaning; one holding
# every word of the question (or the number it names) is kept anyway. Nothing kept: "no related
# documents", and no answer is written.
# GRAPHME_RELEVANCE_FLOOR=0.3
# Hybrid search: the vector (ANN) and fulltext (BM25) rankings fused by weighted reciprocal
# rank fusion. The vector search's weight (the fulltext search gets the rest; a question naming
# a document number gets the two the other way round), and RRF's constant.
# GRAPHME_HYBRID_DENSE_WEIGHT=0.6
# GRAPHME_RRF_K=60
GRAPHME_NODE_BUDGET=24
GRAPHME_TOKEN_BUDGET=6000
GRAPHME_MAX_HOPS=2
